<p>We offer weekly and fortnightly house cleaning in Cottingham for anyone who would rather spend their spare time on something else: working families, shift workers, and older residents who want dependable help around the home. One insured, DBS-checked cleaner looks after your house each visit and follows a checklist built around it, covering the kitchen, bathrooms, dusting, floors and anything else you want prioritised. We supply the equipment and products, and you’ll know the cost before the first clean.</p>
<h3>Cleaning around Cottingham routines</h3>
<p>Plenty of people in Cottingham work at Castle Hill Hospital or the University of Hull, and shift patterns don’t always fit a Monday-to-Friday cleaner. Because we work seven days a week, we can usually find a regular day that suits a rota, weekends included. Commuters heading into Hull by car or by train from Cottingham station often prefer the clean to happen while they’re out, and families with children at the local schools tend to want the house reset before the weekend rather than after it.</p>
<h3>From village-centre terraces to Harland Way</h3>
<p>Cottingham’s homes change from one street to the next. Near Hallgate and King Street there are Victorian and Edwardian terraces and cottages with narrow staircases, small yards and original tiled hallways. Thwaite and Northgate have plenty of inter-war and post-war semis, while the roads off Harland Way and Snuff Mill Lane include larger detached houses with big kitchens, several bathrooms and conservatories that need their glass and frames kept clear of dust. There are also many bungalows across the village, where some owners simply want help with the jobs that involve bending, stretching or carrying the vacuum. Your checklist is agreed at the first visit and can change whenever you like, from extra attention on the bathrooms to fresh bedding every week. Like the rest of the area, Cottingham has hard water, so your cleaner deals with limescale on taps, showers and the kettle every time rather than letting it build.</p>
<h3>Getting started</h3>
<p>If you’ve never had a cleaner before, our guide on <a href="/guides/how-to-choose-a-cleaner/">how to choose a cleaner</a> covers what to ask, and <a href="/guides/preparing-for-your-first-clean/">preparing for your first clean</a> explains what happens on day one. You can give us a key or a key safe code so the clean happens while you’re out, and when your cleaner takes a holiday we send a briefed replacement. Ovens aren’t part of a regular clean, but we can add an <a href="/services/oven-cleaning/">oven clean</a> whenever yours needs one. Skidby and the lanes out towards Little Weighton are covered too, and if you’re just over the hill in the western villages, we also offer <a href="/services/regular-house-cleaning/anlaby-willerby-kirk-ella/">house cleaning in Anlaby, Willerby and Kirk Ella</a>.</p>
<p>Find out more about us on our <a href="/areas/cottingham/">Cottingham area page</a>, or <a href="/contact/">tell us your address and preferred day</a> and we’ll match you with a local cleaner.</p>
